<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kasahrada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1178</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kasahrada was fought in 1178 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-abu">Mount Abu</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, where the Chaulukya army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, led in the name of the young king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mularaja-ii">Mularaja II</a>, defeated the Ghurid sultan Mu'izz al-Din Muhammad. It was his first major defeat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and turned Ghurid expansion towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, where he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> in 1186.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kasahrada.jpg" alt="Battle of Kasahrada" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sajaypal007 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kasahrada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
